<%# Steps for getting an OAuth token from a Claude Pro or Max subscription. %>
<details class="mt-3">
  <summary class="text-text-muted text-xs cursor-pointer hover:text-white transition select-none">
    💡 Using Claude Pro or Max? Get a key without a paid API account
  </summary>
  <div class="mt-2 p-3 bg-surface-overlay rounded-lg border border-border-default text-xs space-y-2">
    <p class="text-text-primary">If you have a <strong class="text-white">Claude Pro or Max</strong> subscription and <strong class="text-white">Claude Code</strong> installed, you can generate an OAuth token instead of an API key:</p>
    <ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-text-muted space-y-1.5 ml-1">
      <li>Open a terminal and run: <code class="text-amber-300 bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">claude setup-token</code></li>
      <li>Follow the prompts to authenticate</li>
      <li>Copy the token it outputs and paste it in the API key field above</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="text-text-faint mt-1">This uses your existing Claude subscription, no separate API billing needed.</p>
    <p class="text-text-faint">Don't have Claude Code? Install it first: <code class="text-amber-300 bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">curl -fsSL https://claude.ai/install.sh | bash</code></p>
  </div>
</details>
